\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {12}{\ignorespaces Status of each chart of the interval atlas: failed boxes in the assembly record, the stored summary counter, the status class computed from the stored summary and checkpoint (budget stop, genuine failures, disposition), the checkpoint counters, and the unprocessed share of the seed transcribed from the review of the records; the column of stack boxes counts the unprocessed boxes in the last checkpoint of a run that stopped at its budget and is a dash for the runs that finished, and a dash elsewhere marks a value that does not exist, as for m1vert-S, which never ran. Here $c_s=r_{35}$ and $t_t=\tan (\theta /2)$, where $\theta \in [0,\pi /2]$ with $\tan \theta =c_s/(u+p)$ is the polar angle of the m2 charts, so that $t_t<1/2$ is $c_s<\tfrac  43(u+p)$.}}{34}{table.caption.95}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:atlas}{{12}{34}{Status of each chart of the interval atlas: failed boxes in the assembly record, the stored summary counter, the status class computed from the stored summary and checkpoint (budget stop, genuine failures, disposition), the checkpoint counters, and the unprocessed share of the seed transcribed from the review of the records; the column of stack boxes counts the unprocessed boxes in the last checkpoint of a run that stopped at its budget and is a dash for the runs that finished, and a dash elsewhere marks a value that does not exist, as for m1vert-S, which never ran. Here $c_s=r_{35}$ and $t_t=\tan (\theta /2)$, where $\theta \in [0,\pi /2]$ with $\tan \theta =c_s/(u+p)$ is the polar angle of the m2 charts, so that $t_t<1/2$ is $c_s<\tfrac 43(u+p)$}{table.caption.95}{}}
